The population and true-factor scope are mostly stated carefully. I’ve found two issues to investigate: the conditional exponent omits the extraction cost’s \(N^{1/6}\) floor, and the moment-barrier remark appears to claim more generality than its citation supports. I’m now checking the fourth-moment error terms and the batched search costs.
