  1478	\section{Experiments}\label{sec:experiments}
  1479	%======================================================================
  1480	
  1481	All experiments were pre-registered: predictions, decision rules, designs and metrics were
  1482	committed before any run. The algorithms see only $N$. The harness samples pairs uniformly from
  1483	$\Sn$ and assigns outcome classes afterwards. Toy-size successes are correctness checks, not
  1484	evidence for exponents.
  1485	
  1486	\subsection{The search \texorpdfstring{$\DCL$}{DCL} (pre-registration \texttt{05d2bf5})}
  1487	\paragraph{Designs.}
  1488	\begin{itemize}
  1489	\item \textbf{C1} is the algorithm of Section~\ref{sec:alg} with a finite-size schedule: $H$
  1490	  minimal with block-0 multiplicity $\lambda_0\ge3$, so $H\asymp\sqrt n$. At this $H$ the
  1491	  proved exceptional bounds exceed $1$ and are vacuous. The experiments therefore test
  1492	  correctness, the lemmas and the cost exponent, not the proved rate.
  1493	\item \textbf{C2} is C1 with $\lambda_0\ge\ln(P/\ln P)+2$ (heuristically full coverage), up to
  1494	  64 bits.
  1495	\item \textbf{C3} is C1 with all odd band primes, Tonelli--Shanks roots and a charged
  1496	  nonresidue search.
  1497	\item \textbf{HH} is a calibrated Harvey--Hittmeir implementation.
  1498	\end{itemize}
  1499	
  1500	\paragraph{Metric.} The cost proxy $E$ counts $n$-bit modular-multiplication equivalents, with
  1501	polynomial work charged as $\sum(D+1)\lceil\log_2(D+2)\rceil$. $E_{\mathrm{first}}$ counts the
  1502	blocks up to the first success.
  1503	
  1504	\paragraph{Lemma checks (28--40 bits, 240 pairs).}
  1505	\begin{itemize}
  1506	\item All 240 pairs were correct and factored.
  1507	\item There were 0 violations of Lemmas~\ref{lem:lock}--\ref{lem:modq}.
  1508	\item There were 0 violations of ``gcd $=p$ iff not FULL'' on 3002 clean covering targets.
  1509	\end{itemize}
  1510	
  1511	\paragraph{Cost (40--80 bits).}
  1512	\begin{center}
  1513	\footnotesize
  1514	\begin{tabular}{rrrrrr}
  1515	\toprule
  1516	$n$ & $H/Y$ & succ. & C1 $E_{\mathrm{first}}$ & HH $E$ & C1/HH\\
  1517	\midrule
  1518	40 & 9/81 & 32/32 & $1.03\cdot10^5$ & $2.12\cdot10^4$ & 4.87\\
  1519	48 & 9/206 & 32/32 & $3.26\cdot10^5$ & $7.57\cdot10^4$ & 4.31\\
  1520	56 & 10/503 & 32/32 & $1.01\cdot10^6$ & $2.96\cdot10^5$ & 3.40\\
  1521	64 & 11/1461 & 32/32 & $4.08\cdot10^6$ & $9.43\cdot10^5$ & 4.33\\
  1522	72 & 11/3097 & 32/32 & $1.06\cdot10^7$ & $3.43\cdot10^6$ & 3.10\\
  1523	80 & 11/7804 & 32/32 & $2.76\cdot10^7$ & $1.18\cdot10^7$ & 2.35\\
  1524	\bottomrule
  1525	\end{tabular}
  1526	\end{center}
  1527	\begin{itemize}
  1528	\item Over 48--80 bits, the least-squares slopes of $\log_2$ of the median $E_{\mathrm{first}}$
  1529	  are $0.203$ (C1), $0.196$ (C3), $0.227$ (C2, 48--64 bits) and $0.226$ (HH).
  1530	\item There were 0 incorrect outputs in 656 runs.
  1531	\item With heuristically full coverage (C2) there is no slope advantage.
  1532	\item The slope difference partly reflects the $H$ schedule, and slopes are not exponents.
  1533	\item Over 48--96 bits (1000 pairs per size), uncovered and clean fractions match the Poisson
  1534	  and $1-\sum1/(\ell-1)$ predictions, and FULL occurred on at most $0.045\%$ of covering targets.
  1535	\end{itemize}
  1536	
  1537	\subsection{Coverage statistics (pre-registration of \texttt{sieve2d})}
  1538	\begin{itemize}
  1539	\item The design was 228 cells of $10^6$ sampled pairs at 48--96 bits, plus 620 exhaustive cells
  1540	  at 20--30 bits.
  1541	\item Uncovered counts matched the independent-residue model, with pooled ratio $1.00001$ over
  1542	  202 cells. The decay was exponential, with fitted slope $-0.9995$ in $\lambda_{\mathrm{eff}}$.
  1543	  Prime and integer pairs agreed to $1.00004$.
  1544	\item One frozen prediction failed: the fourth moment for \emph{integer} pairs, through a
  1545	  heavy-tailed atom at $x\equiv(0,0)$. Every prime cell passed.
  1546	\item Exploratory sixth moments for prime pairs were within $[0.961,1.038]$ of the model.
  1547	\item These data support the conjectural $e^{-\lambda}$ regime. They do not test the proved rate.
  1548	\end{itemize}
  1549	
  1550	\subsection{Worst-case coverage and Theorem~\ref{thm:Rprecise} (pre-registration of \texttt{dchworst})}
  1551	\begin{itemize}
  1552	\item The worst-case weight height over all $6.2\cdot10^6$ pairs of $\mathcal S_{32}$ and
  1553	  $7.8\cdot10^7$ pairs of $\mathcal S_{36}$ follows the Poisson extreme in all 8 fits. Three
  1554	  frozen predictions failed: one was mis-stated, one failed with the model's own expected number of
  1555	  exceedances, and one failed only on the side of better-than-random coverage.
  1556	\item $\DCLwc$ had 0 failures on covered pairs, exhaustively over $\mathcal S_{26}$ and
  1557	  $\mathcal S_{28}$ (about $6.5\cdot10^5$ pairs) and on 36 adversarial cells. These included
  1558	  equal orders of $2$ modulo $p$ and $q$, small $\ord_q(2)$ and FULL-forcing families. The
  1559	  algorithm of Section~\ref{sec:alg} failed on 153 of these covered pairs.
  1560	\end{itemize}
