   997	\subsection{Where this method stops}
   998	The following remark explains why the method stops at $\lambda^{-2}$.
   999	
  1000	\begin{remark}[a moment barrier; proved for its stated scope]\label{rem:PYY}
  1001	Fix $J\ge2$. Peled, Yadin and Yehudayoff \cite[Cor.~1.2(1), 1.3(1)]{pyy2011} construct $J$-wise
  1002	independent Bernoulli variables with prescribed marginals and $\Pr(\text{all }0)\ge
  1003	c_J\lambda^{-\lfloor J/2\rfloor}$. Attach to each event a uniform label in $V$. Then all labelled
  1004	event statistics of order at most $J$ agree exactly with the independent model, while the
  1005	uncovered mass is $\ge c_J\lambda^{-\lfloor J/2\rfloor}$. So no argument whose only input is the
  1006	joint distribution of at most $J$ band-prime events can prove $o(\lambda^{-\lfloor J/2\rfloor})$.
  1007	
  1008	Our error analysis controls $J\le4$; $J=5$ is sketched in the notes, and by the above it cannot
  1009	improve on $\lambda^{-2}$. At $J=6$ the per-lattice error bounds add up to about $\Xb^2/H^2$,
  1010	far above the target $\Xb^2\lambda^{-3}$. This is a limit of this proof technique, not of the
  1168	  \end{itemize}
