  1174	\begin{theorem}[precise form of Theorem~\ref{thm:R}; proved]\label{thm:Rprecise}
  1175	Let $N=pq\in\Sn$. Then:
  1176	\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
  1177	\item $\DCLwc$ outputs a proper divisor of $N$ or \texttt{FAIL};
  1178	\item if $(p,q)$ is covered by $(\mathcal P_k,V)$ for some $k$, it outputs a proper divisor;
  1179	\item its cost is
  1180	\[
  1181	  \tilde O\Bigl(\sum_k(m_k+T'_k+|V||\mathcal P_k|+|\mathcal P_k|\log Y)+B_0T^{1/2}+\sqrt N/T
  1182	  +\sqrt N/\Psi(\sqrt{N/2}-1,B_0)\Bigr)
  1183	\]
  1184	ring operations modulo $N$, plus $\tilde O(|V||\mathcal P_k|)$ word operations. Here $\Psi$
  1185	counts smooth numbers. With $T=\lceil N^{1/3}\rceil$ and $B_0=\lceil n^4\rceil$, the last three
  1186	terms are $N^{1/6}n^{O(1)}$.
