  1271	\begin{proof}[Proof of Corollary~\ref{cor:conditional}]
  1272	\begin{itemize}
  1273	\item \emph{(a).} Apply Theorem~\ref{thm:Rprecise} with the design of $\DCL_{n,H}$ and signed
  1274	  weights. The list cost is $n^{O(1)}H^{5/3}2^{n/6}=N^{1/6+o(1)}$.
  1275	\item \emph{(b).} Apply Theorem~\ref{thm:Rprecise} with one block, the $J$ primes, and all
  1276	  signed weights of height $H$. With $J=Y^{j}$ and $H=Y^{1/2}J^{-c}$ the list cost is
  1277	  $HP/Y^2+JH^2$, which is balanced at $Y=N^{1/(5+2j(1-c))}$ with exponent
  1278	  $E(j,c)=(1+j(1-2c))/(5+2j(1-c))$. Since $\partial_jE$ has the sign of $3-8c$, for $c>3/8$ the
  1279	  best choice is $j=1$, which gives $Y=N^{1/(7-2c)}$ and $(1-c)/(7/2-c)$. The extraction overhead
  1280	  of Theorem~\ref{thm:Rprecise} is $N^{1/6+o(1)}$, which does not exceed this.
  1281	\end{itemize}
  1282	\end{proof}
