  1704	\begin{theorem}[full-candidate floors; proved in the model]\label{thm:A}
  1705	Every covering family has $X\ge cN^{1/6}$. If degree-one targets cover fewer than half the
  1706	candidates, then $X\ge cN^{1/5}$. If the degree-one two-term targets use $J$ moduli, then
  1707	$X\ge cN^{1/5}(JN^{o(1)})^{-1/5}$.
